LIB_LOAD("mu",{"mu1":{"challenge":[{"q":"In which region of South Africa was Murray born?","o":["The Karoo","Lagos","The Sahara","Scotland"],"why":"In Graaff-Reinet."},{"q":"What did Murray's father pray for every Friday?","o":["Revival","Rain only","Money","A new house"],"why":"For years and years."},{"q":"About how many books did Murray write?","o":["More than two hundred","One","Five","Ten"],"why":"Many on prayer."},{"q":"Who prayed at the 1860 youth meeting in Worcester?","o":["A young servant girl","The king","A bishop","A soldier"],"why":"And revival spread."},{"q":"Joel 2:28 says God will pour out His Spirit upon...?","o":["All flesh","Only kings","Only priests","Nobody"],"why":"Sons and daughters too."},{"q":"What did the disciples ask Jesus?","o":["Lord, teach us to pray","Lord, teach us to fish","Lord, make us rich","Lord, let us rest"],"why":"Luke 11:1."},{"q":"What's the first lesson in the school of prayer?","o":["Admit you need the Teacher","Pray very long prayers","Use big words","Pray loudly"],"why":"Lord, teach me."},{"q":"Where did Jesus say to pray in secret?","o":["In your closet, with the door shut","On the street","On a rooftop","In the market"],"why":"Matthew 6:6."},{"q":"\"Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be...\"","o":["thy name","my name","the day","the king"],"why":"Matthew 6:9."},{"q":"How long did Ladi spend in her secret place?","o":["Ten minutes","Ten hours","One second","All day"],"why":"The best ten minutes of her day."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! In which country did Andrew Murray study after Scotland?","o":["Holland (the Netherlands)","Nigeria","America","China"],"why":"Before coming home as a minister in 1848."},"choices":[{"title":"Same old words","q":"You say exactly the same prayer every night without thinking about it.","o":[{"t":"Ask, 'Lord, teach me to pray,' and talk to Him honestly about your day.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Every pupil starts by asking the Teacher."},{"t":"Stop praying because it feels boring.","f":"The Teacher can make it come alive."},{"t":"Say it faster.","f":"Prayer is a conversation, not a race."}]},{"title":"Too young to matter","q":"Your youth group is praying for your town, and you think, \"My prayer won't change anything.\"","o":[{"t":"Pray anyway, with your whole heart.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! A revival began with a servant girl's prayer."},{"t":"Let the adults do it.","f":"God pours out His Spirit on sons and daughters too."},{"t":"Stay quiet and think about lunch.","f":"Your prayer matters to God."}]},{"title":"No quiet place","q":"Your home is always busy and loud. You can never pray alone.","o":[{"t":"Find a time or place, like early morning or a walk, to be alone with God.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Shut the door on the world and open it to your Father."},{"t":"Give up on personal prayer.","f":"A secret place can be anywhere."},{"t":"Only pray at church.","f":"Your Father wants to meet you every day."}]},{"title":"Scared of God","q":"You feel nervous praying, as if God is a stern headteacher.","o":[{"t":"Remember Jesus taught you to start with 'Father'.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! He's a loving Father who's glad to see you."},{"t":"Avoid praying.","f":"Your Father is waiting for you."},{"t":"Only pray when in trouble.","f":"Talk with Him every day, like a child to a father."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"karoo","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 1 of With Christ in the School of Prayer in real life."},{"sc":"church","n":"🔥 Your prayers matter, however young you are."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"🎒 Ask the best Teacher: 'Lord, teach me to pray.'"},{"sc":"prayercloset","n":"🚪 Find a secret place and shut the door on distractions."},{"sc":"prayercloset","n":"❤️ Start with 'Father'. He's glad to see you."}],"stops":{"mu1s1":{"story":[{"sc":"karoo","n":"In 1828, in the dry, dusty Karoo of South Africa, a boy called {Andrew Murray} was born in the town of {Graaff-Reinet}."},{"sc":"karoo","n":"His father was a pastor who had come from Scotland. Every Friday evening, his father did something the children never forgot."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murraysr","e":"smile","t":"Lord, pour out Your Spirit on this land. Send {revival}! Turn many hearts to You."},{"sc":"karoo","n":"For years and years, he read stories of revivals and prayed for one, week after week. Andrew grew up listening."},{"sc":"karoo","n":"When Andrew was ten, he and his brother John were sent all the way to Scotland for school. Later they studied in Holland. In 1848, at just twenty, Andrew came home as a young minister."},{"sc":"karoo","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"My first church covered a huge area. I rode on horseback for days to visit families scattered across the land. I preached, I taught, I baptised. But I still had a lot to learn about prayer."},{"sc":"study","n":"Over his long life, Andrew Murray wrote more than two hundred books. One of the most loved is a book of short lessons called With Christ in the School of Prayer."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"big","t":"In this book, I'm not your teacher. Jesus is. I'm just a fellow pupil sitting in His class with you. Shall we learn together?"}],"quote":{"text":"O thou that hearest prayer, unto thee shall all flesh come.","who":"Psalm 65:2","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"A father's prayers","text":"Andrew Murray grew up watching his father pray for revival every Friday for years. He became a pastor and wrote over two hundred books, many on prayer. But he said the real Teacher of prayer is Jesus."},"think":"Who in your life prays faithfully? What have you learned from watching them?","quiz":[{"q":"Where was Andrew Murray born?","o":["Graaff-Reinet, South Africa","London","Lagos","New York"],"why":"In the dry Karoo, in 1828."},{"q":"What did his father do every Friday evening?","o":["Pray for revival","Play cricket","Go to market","Write letters"],"why":"For years and years."},{"q":"Where was Andrew sent to school at age ten?","o":["Scotland","America","Nigeria","Australia"],"why":"With his brother John."},{"q":"How did young Andrew visit families in his first church?","o":["On horseback for days","By train","By car","He didn't visit"],"why":"A huge area."},{"q":"Who did Murray say is the real teacher of prayer?","o":["Jesus","Murray himself","His father","Nobody"],"why":"We're all pupils."}]},"mu1s2":{"story":[{"sc":"church","n":"In 1860, Andrew Murray was the pastor in the town of {Worcester}. News had come of revivals in America and Scotland, and people across South Africa began praying."},{"sc":"church","n":"One Sunday evening, a group of young people gathered for a prayer meeting. Several prayed. Then a young servant girl, about fifteen years old, stood up and asked if she could pray."},{"sc":"church","w":"amgirl","e":"big","t":"Lord, come and move among us tonight. We need You!"},{"sc":"church","n":"She prayed simply, with her whole heart. Nobody now remembers her exact words. But everyone remembered what happened next."},{"sc":"church","n":"As she prayed, the people say they heard a sound like distant thunder coming closer. Suddenly, everyone in the room was praying aloud at the same time. Some wept. Some cried out to God."},{"sc":"church","n":"Andrew Murray arrived and was alarmed. It was noisy and unusual. He tried to calm everyone down. But the praying went on."},{"sc":"church","n":"The story is told that a visitor quietly said to him: 'Be careful what you do. I believe it is the Spirit of God at work here.'"},{"sc":"church","w":"murray","e":"worried","t":"I had to learn that God can work in ways I don't expect. He can even begin a revival through the prayer of a young servant girl."},{"sc":"karoo","n":"Prayer meetings sprang up night after night, and the revival spread to many towns. Over the following years, many young men offered themselves to become pastors and missionaries. Andrew's father had prayed for this for years. God answered."}],"quote":{"text":"And it shall come to pass afterward, that I will pour out my spirit upon all flesh; and your sons and your daughters shall prophesy.","who":"Joel 2:28","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"God uses young people's prayers","text":"The 1860 revival in Worcester began, as the story is told, when a teenage servant girl prayed. God doesn't need you to be old, important or eloquent. A young person who prays with a whole heart can be the spark."},"think":"Do you ever think your prayers don't matter because you're young? What does this story say?","quiz":[{"q":"In what year did the Worcester revival begin?","o":["1860","1760","1960","1828"],"why":"Andrew Murray was pastor there."},{"q":"Who stood up to pray at the youth meeting?","o":["A young servant girl","The mayor","Andrew Murray","A soldier"],"why":"About fifteen years old."},{"q":"What happened as she prayed?","o":["Everyone began praying aloud","Everyone left","Nothing","They started singing a hymn"],"why":"Some wept and cried out to God."},{"q":"How did Andrew Murray react at first?","o":["He was alarmed and tried to calm everyone","He joined in at once","He went home","He laughed"],"why":"He had to learn God works in unexpected ways."},{"q":"Who had prayed for revival for years?","o":["Andrew's father","The servant girl's boss","The king","Nobody"],"why":"Every Friday evening."}]},"mu1s3":{"story":[{"sc":"mountside","n":"Long ago, Jesus' disciples watched Him. Often, He went off alone early in the morning or late at night to pray. When He came back, there was something different about Him."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"amdisciple","e":"worried","t":"Lord, teach us to pray, as John also taught his disciples."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"Notice something. They never asked Jesus, 'Teach us to preach' or 'Teach us to do miracles.' They asked, 'Teach us to pray.' They could see prayer was the secret behind everything He did."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"This is where the school of prayer begins. Jesus is the teacher. And the very first lesson is to admit: I don't know how to pray as I should. Lord, teach me."},{"sc":"home","w":"amemeka","e":"worried","t":"Honestly, I never know what to say when I pray. I just say the same words every night before I sleep."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Then you're in exactly the right place, Emeka! Every pupil starts as a beginner. Even the disciples did. Just come to class and ask the Teacher."},{"sc":"home","w":"amladi","e":"smile","t":"So the best first prayer is: 'Lord, teach me to pray.'"}],"quote":{"text":"And it came to pass, that, as he was praying in a certain place, when he ceased, one of his disciples said unto him, Lord, teach us to pray.","who":"Luke 11:1","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Everyone starts as a beginner","text":"The disciples saw that prayer was Jesus' secret, so they asked: 'Lord, teach us to pray.' Murray says that's the first lesson. Don't worry if you don't know what to say. Come to class and ask the Teacher."},"think":"Pray this simple prayer today: 'Lord, teach me to pray.' Then notice how He answers this week.","quiz":[{"q":"What did the disciples see Jesus doing?","o":["Going off alone to pray","Sleeping a lot","Fishing all day","Writing books"],"why":"Early in the morning or late at night."},{"q":"What did the disciples ask Jesus to teach them?","o":["To pray","To preach","To do miracles","To fish"],"why":"Prayer was His secret."},{"q":"Who is the teacher in the school of prayer?","o":["Jesus","Andrew Murray","Emeka","John the Baptist"],"why":"Murray is just a fellow pupil."},{"q":"What was Emeka's problem with prayer?","o":["He never knew what to say","He prayed too long","He didn't believe in God","He had no time"],"why":"Same words every night."},{"q":"According to Ladi, what's the best first prayer?","o":["'Lord, teach me to pray'","'Give me money'","Nothing","'Make me famous'"],"why":"Ask the Teacher!"}]},"mu1s4":{"story":[{"sc":"mountside","w":"amjesus","e":"smile","t":"But thou, when thou prayest, enter into thy closet, and when thou hast shut thy door, pray to thy Father which is in secret; and thy Father which seeth in secret shall reward thee openly."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"amjesus","e":"smile","t":"After this manner therefore pray ye: Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Two lessons in one! First: find a secret place. Shut the door on noise and distractions. It's you and God, alone."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"big","t":"Second: notice the very first word Jesus taught us to say: Father! Prayer isn't a stranger talking to a stern judge. It's a child talking to a loving Father who's glad to see them."},{"sc":"home","w":"amladi","e":"worried","t":"My house is so busy and noisy. Where can I be alone?"},{"sc":"home","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"It doesn't have to be a special room. Some people pray on a walk, or early before anyone wakes, or with a cloth over their head. What matters is shutting the door on the world for a little while, and opening the door to your Father."},{"sc":"prayercloset","n":"Ladi began waking ten minutes earlier. She sat on the back step, before the house woke up, and talked to her Father. It became the best ten minutes of her day."}],"quote":{"text":"And thy Father which seeth in secret shall reward thee openly.","who":"Matthew 6:6","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Shut the door, say 'Father'","text":"Jesus taught: find a secret place, shut the door, and begin with 'Our Father'. Prayer isn't talking to a stranger. It's a child talking with a loving Father who's glad to see them. Even ten quiet minutes can become the best part of your day."},"think":"Where could your 'secret place' be? When could you be there for ten minutes tomorrow?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did Jesus say to go when you pray?","o":["Into your closet, with the door shut","To the market","On a stage","Into a crowd"],"why":"Matthew 6:6."},{"q":"What's the first word of the prayer Jesus taught?","o":["Our (Father)","Give","Please","Lord"],"why":"Our Father which art in heaven."},{"q":"What did Murray say prayer is like?","o":["A child talking to a loving Father","A stranger talking to a judge","A test","A speech"],"why":"He's glad to see you."},{"q":"Does your secret place have to be a special room?","o":["No, it can be a walk or an early morning","Yes, always","It must be in church","It must be outdoors"],"why":"Shut the door on the world for a while."},{"q":"Where did Ladi pray each morning?","o":["On the back step before the house woke up","In the kitchen at noon","At school","On the bus"],"why":"The best ten minutes of her day."}]}}},"mu2":{"challenge":[{"q":"\"Ask, and it shall be...\"","o":["given you","taken away","forgotten","hidden"],"why":"Matthew 7:7."},{"q":"\"Every one that asketh...\"","o":["receiveth","waiteth","loseth","sleepeth"],"why":"Matthew 7:8."},{"q":"Which Igbo proverb is about asking?","o":["The one who asks never gets lost","Pride is a turban","Words are eggs","A patient man cooks a stone"],"why":"Onye ajụjụ anaghị efu ụzọ."},{"q":"No father gives his son a ___ when he asks for bread.","o":["stone","loaf","fish","cup"],"why":"Matthew 7:9."},{"q":"What three words show God's generosity in Matthew 7:11?","o":["How much more","Not so much","Maybe a little","Only sometimes"],"why":"Your Father in heaven."},{"q":"How many loaves did the man at midnight ask for?","o":["Three","One","Five","Twelve"],"why":"Luke 11:5."},{"q":"What word means 'not giving up when you ask'?","o":["Importunity","Impatience","Importance","Impossibility"],"why":"Luke 11:8."},{"q":"Who shouted 'Jesus, thou son of David, have mercy on me!'?","o":["Bartimaeus","Peter","Zacchaeus","Nicodemus"],"why":"Outside Jericho."},{"q":"What did Bartimaeus ask for?","o":["His sight","Money","Food","A house"],"why":"And he received it."},{"q":"What did Bartimaeus do after he could see?","o":["Followed Jesus","Went home","Sat back down","Ran away"],"why":"Mark 10:52."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What did Bartimaeus throw off when Jesus called him?","o":["His cloak","His shoes","His hat","His bag"],"why":"He jumped up and came to Jesus."},"choices":[{"title":"Shy to ask","q":"You need help with something big, but you think God is too busy for your small problems.","o":[{"t":"Ask Him anyway. Jesus said every one that asks receives.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Ask, seek, knock."},{"t":"Sort it out alone.","f":"Your Father wants you to ask."},{"t":"Only pray for big things.","f":"Nothing is too small for a loving Father."}]},{"title":"Doubting God's heart","q":"You worry that if you ask God for something, He'll give you something bad instead.","o":[{"t":"Remember: no good father gives a stone for bread, and God is much better.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! How much more!"},{"t":"Stop asking, just in case.","f":"God is a generous Father."},{"t":"Only ask for things you don't care about.","f":"He wants to hear your real requests."}]},{"title":"Still no answer","q":"You've prayed for months for your parents to stop arguing, and nothing seems to change.","o":[{"t":"Keep praying, and talk to a trusted adult about how you feel.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Keep knocking, and don't carry it alone."},{"t":"Decide prayer doesn't work.","f":"Sometimes God says 'wait' while He works."},{"t":"Blame yourself.","f":"It's not your fault. Bring it to your Father."}]},{"title":"Bless everyone","q":"Your prayers are always the same: \"God, bless everyone. Amen.\"","o":[{"t":"Make a short prayer list with specific requests.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Be definite, like Bartimaeus."},{"t":"Keep it vague.","f":"Jesus asks: what do you want me to do?"},{"t":"Stop praying for others.","f":"Pray for them, by name and need."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"mountside","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 2 of With Christ in the School of Prayer in real life."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"🗝️ Ask, seek, knock. Every one that asks receives."},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"🎁 God is a better Father than the best dad: how much more!"},{"sc":"knockdoor","n":"🚪 Keep knocking. Don't give up."},{"sc":"jerichoroad","n":"🎯 Be specific. Tell Jesus what you want Him to do."}],"stops":{"mu2s1":{"story":[{"sc":"mountside","n":"On a hillside in Galilee, crowds sat on the grass to listen to Jesus teach."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"amjesus","e":"big","t":"Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"amjesus","e":"smile","t":"For every one that asketh receiveth; and he that seeketh findeth; and to him that knocketh it shall be opened."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Did you notice how many times He said it? Ask, seek, knock. Then: every one that asks, receives. Jesus wanted us to be absolutely sure that prayer is heard."},{"sc":"home","w":"amemeka","e":"worried","t":"But I feel bad asking God for things. Isn't that selfish? Shouldn't I just accept whatever happens?"},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Emeka, Jesus Himself told you to ask! A child who never asks his father for anything doesn't trust him much, does he? Asking shows that you believe God is real, and that He cares."},{"sc":"home","w":"amladi","e":"smile","t":"Emeka, your grandma always says something in Igbo: the person who asks questions never gets lost on the road."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"big","t":"Wise grandma! Don't be shy with your Father. Ask, seek, knock."}],"quote":{"text":"Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you.","who":"Matthew 7:7","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Jesus says: ask!","text":"Jesus told us three times to ask, seek and knock, and promised that everyone who asks receives. Asking God isn't selfish. It shows you trust Him. Don't be shy with your Father."},"think":"Is there something you've never asked God for because you felt shy or unsure? Ask Him today.","proverb":{"text":"Onye ajụjụ anaghị efu ụzọ.","lang":"Igbo","mean":"The person who asks questions never gets lost. Don't be too proud or shy to ask."},"quiz":[{"q":"What three things did Jesus tell us to do?","o":["Ask, seek, knock","Sit, stand, run","Read, write, count","Eat, sleep, play"],"why":"Matthew 7:7."},{"q":"According to Jesus, who receives?","o":["Every one that asks","Only rich people","Only adults","Nobody"],"why":"Matthew 7:8."},{"q":"Why did Emeka feel bad asking God for things?","o":["He thought it was selfish","He didn't believe in God","He was angry","He was too busy"],"why":"But Jesus told us to ask!"},{"q":"What did Murray say asking shows?","o":["That you trust God is real and cares","That you're greedy","That you're weak","Nothing"],"why":"Like a child asking a father."},{"q":"What does the Igbo proverb say about someone who asks questions?","o":["They never get lost","They're annoying","They're foolish","They're slow"],"why":"Onye ajụjụ anaghị efu ụzọ."}]},"mu2s2":{"story":[{"sc":"mountside","w":"amjesus","e":"smile","t":"Or what man is there of you, whom if his son ask bread, will he give him a stone? Or if he ask a fish, will he give him a serpent?"},{"sc":"mountside","n":"The crowd laughed. Of course no father would do that!"},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"That evening, Ladi asked her dad if he could help her with her science project."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"amdad","e":"smile","t":"Of course, my daughter! And I bought you the coloured card you needed on my way home. Here."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"amladi","e":"big","t":"Thanks, Dad! You're the best."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"amjesus","e":"big","t":"If ye then, being evil, know how to give good gifts unto your children, how much more shall your Father which is in heaven give good things to them that ask him?"},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"How much more! Think of the kindest, most generous father you know. God is more generous than that. Much, much more."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"And if your own earthly father has let you down, God is the Father you always needed. He never gives a stone when you ask for bread."}],"quote":{"text":"Or what man is there of you, whom if his son ask bread, will he give him a stone?","who":"Matthew 7:9","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"A better Father","text":"No good father gives a stone when his child asks for bread. Jesus said: how much more will your Father in heaven give good things! Even the kindest dad is only a small picture of God's generous heart."},"think":"What do you know about God's heart from the way the best parents treat their children?","quiz":[{"q":"What does a father NOT give when his son asks for bread?","o":["A stone","Bread","Water","A hug"],"why":"No good father would!"},{"q":"What would a father not give instead of a fish?","o":["A serpent","A fish","A boat","A net"],"why":"Matthew 7:10."},{"q":"What had Ladi's dad already bought her?","o":["Coloured card for her project","A phone","A bike","Nothing"],"why":"He was generous."},{"q":"What are the key words in Matthew 7:11?","o":["How much more","Not at all","Only a little","Never again"],"why":"God is more generous still."},{"q":"If your earthly father let you down, what did Murray say about God?","o":["He is the Father you always needed","He's the same","He's far away","He doesn't care"],"why":"He never gives a stone for bread."}]},"mu2s3":{"story":[{"sc":"knockdoor","n":"Jesus told a story. It was midnight. A man had a guest arrive from a long journey, and there was no food in his house. So he ran to his neighbour's door."},{"sc":"knockdoor","w":"amfriend","e":"worried","t":"Friend, lend me three loaves! A friend of mine has come, and I have nothing to set before him!"},{"sc":"knockdoor","w":"amneighbour","e":"frown","t":"Trouble me not: the door is now shut, and my children are with me in bed; I cannot rise and give thee."},{"sc":"knockdoor","w":"amfriend","e":"big","t":"Please! I need bread! Please!"},{"sc":"knockdoor","n":"He kept knocking. And knocking. Finally the neighbour grumbled, got up, and gave him all the bread he needed, just because he wouldn't stop asking."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Now, Jesus isn't saying God is a grumpy neighbour! He's saying: if even a sleepy neighbour gives because of {importunity}, how much more will your loving Father? So keep asking, boldly. Don't give up."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"My father prayed for revival every week for years before the answer came. Sometimes God answers at once. Sometimes He says 'wait', because He's growing something in us while we ask. And sometimes He gives something better than we asked for."},{"sc":"home","w":"amemeka","e":"smile","t":"So if I've been praying for my uncle to know Jesus for a whole year... I shouldn't stop."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"big","t":"Never stop! Keep knocking."}],"quote":{"text":"And he shall answer and say, Trouble me not: the door is now shut, and my children are with me in bed; I cannot rise and give thee.","who":"Luke 11:7","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Keep knocking","text":"The man kept knocking at midnight until his neighbour gave him bread. God isn't grumpy like the neighbour, but Jesus wants us to keep asking boldly. Sometimes God answers at once, sometimes 'wait'. Don't stop knocking."},"think":"What have you been praying about for a long time? How does this story encourage you to keep going?","quiz":[{"q":"What time did the man knock on his neighbour's door?","o":["Midnight","Noon","Breakfast time","Sunset"],"why":"A guest had arrived."},{"q":"What did he ask for?","o":["Three loaves","A fish","Money","A lamp"],"why":"He had nothing to set before his guest."},{"q":"Why did the neighbour finally get up?","o":["Because the man wouldn't stop asking","Because he was hungry","Because of the noise of the children","Because it was morning"],"why":"His importunity."},{"q":"Is God like the grumpy neighbour?","o":["No; if even he gives, how much more will God","Yes","Sometimes","Only at night"],"why":"Keep asking a loving Father."},{"q":"What did Murray say God sometimes answers?","o":["'Wait', or something better than we asked","Never anything","Always exactly what we want, at once","Only on Sundays"],"why":"He grows something in us as we ask."}]},"mu2s4":{"story":[{"sc":"jerichoroad","n":"By the road outside Jericho sat a blind beggar called {Bartimaeus}. One day, he heard a crowd coming. Someone said, 'It's Jesus of Nazareth!'"},{"sc":"jerichoroad","w":"ambart","e":"big","t":"Jesus, thou son of David, have mercy on me!"},{"sc":"jerichoroad","n":"People told him to be quiet. But he shouted even louder. Jesus stopped, and called for him. Bartimaeus threw off his cloak and jumped up."},{"sc":"jerichoroad","w":"amjesus","e":"smile","t":"What wilt thou that I should do unto thee?"},{"sc":"jerichoroad","w":"ambart","e":"worried","t":"Lord, that I might receive my sight."},{"sc":"jerichoroad","w":"amjesus","e":"smile","t":"Go thy way; thy faith hath made thee whole."},{"sc":"jerichoroad","n":"Immediately he could see! And he followed Jesus along the road."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Jesus knew what Bartimaeus needed. But He still asked: what do you want? He wants us to be definite: to know what we're asking and say it plainly."},{"sc":"home","w":"amladi","e":"smile","t":"I usually pray 'God, bless everyone.' Maybe I should write a list instead: 'Help Mum find work. Heal Emeka's grandma's leg. Help me forgive Joy.'"},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"big","t":"Yes! Then you'll be able to see His answers too, and thank Him for each one."}],"quote":{"text":"And Jesus said unto him, Go thy way; thy faith hath made thee whole. And immediately he received his sight, and followed Jesus in the way.","who":"Mark 10:52","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Say what you mean","text":"Jesus asked Bartimaeus, 'What do you want me to do?' Bartimaeus answered plainly: 'That I might see.' Murray says prayer should be definite. Make a prayer list, ask clearly, and watch for His answers."},"think":"Write a short prayer list with three specific requests. Check back in a month to see how God has answered.","quiz":[{"q":"Where did Bartimaeus sit?","o":["By the road outside Jericho","In the temple","In a boat","On a mountain"],"why":"A blind beggar."},{"q":"What did people tell Bartimaeus to do?","o":["Be quiet","Shout louder","Go home","Run"],"why":"But he shouted louder!"},{"q":"What did Jesus ask him?","o":["What wilt thou that I should do unto thee?","Who are you?","Where are you going?","Why are you here?"],"why":"Mark 10:51."},{"q":"What did Murray say prayer should be?","o":["Definite","Vague","Long","Silent"],"why":"Say plainly what you're asking."},{"q":"What did Ladi decide to make?","o":["A prayer list","A cake","A video","A poster"],"why":"Then she can see His answers."}]}}},"mu3":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did the fig tree have plenty of?","o":["Leaves","Fruit","Birds","Flowers"],"why":"But no fruit."},{"q":"What did Jesus say after the fig tree withered?","o":["Have faith in God","Plant more trees","Go home","Be careful"],"why":"Mark 11:22."},{"q":"Faith, according to Murray, looks at...?","o":["God","The problem","Our feelings","Other people"],"why":"How great and good He is."},{"q":"What did Jesus say faith could cast into the sea?","o":["A mountain","A boat","A net","A tree"],"why":"Mark 11:23."},{"q":"1 John 5:14: God hears us if we ask according to...?","o":["His will","our wishes","our feelings","our friends"],"why":"That's our confidence."},{"q":"What did Emeka pray for before speaking at assembly?","o":["Wisdom and courage","A phone","A holiday","Rain"],"why":"A promise from James."},{"q":"When you stand praying, Jesus says...?","o":["Forgive","Complain","Hurry","Shout"],"why":"Mark 11:25."},{"q":"Who forgot to open the door for Peter?","o":["Rhoda","Mary","Joy","Ladi"],"why":"Acts 12."},{"q":"Where two or three are gathered in Jesus' name, He is...?","o":["In the midst of them","Far away","Asleep","Busy"],"why":"Matthew 18:20."},{"q":"If two of you shall ___ on earth, it shall be done.","o":["agree","argue","sleep","run"],"why":"Matthew 18:19."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What does 'Àjèjé ọwọ́ kan kò gbé ẹrù dórí' mean?","o":["One hand alone can't lift a load onto the head","Hands are for clapping","Work alone","Carry nothing"],"why":"Pray together!"},"choices":[{"title":"Worry spiral","q":"You can't stop thinking about an upcoming exam, and you feel sick with worry.","o":[{"t":"Study well, and pray by looking at who God is, not just at the exam.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Have faith in God."},{"t":"Keep worrying all night.","f":"Look away from the problem, to God."},{"t":"Don't study; just pray for a miracle.","f":"Faith and hard work go together."}]},{"title":"Magic prayer?","q":"A friend says, \"If you really believe, God has to give you whatever you want.\"","o":[{"t":"Explain that we pray with confidence for what fits God's will and promises.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! According to His will, He hears us."},{"t":"Agree and pray for a car.","f":"Faith isn't a magic trick."},{"t":"Decide prayer is pointless.","f":"Faith stands on God's promises."}]},{"title":"Still angry","q":"You're about to pray, but you're still furious with a friend who hurt you.","o":[{"t":"Ask God to help you forgive them, then pray.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! When ye stand praying, forgive."},{"t":"Pray that they get what they deserve.","f":"Prayer and love go together."},{"t":"Skip praying until you're less angry.","f":"Bring the anger to God. He'll help."}]},{"title":"Praying alone","q":"You want to pray for your school, but feel like you're the only one.","o":[{"t":"Invite one or two friends to pray with you each week.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Where two or three are gathered, He's there."},{"t":"Give up.","f":"One hand can't lift the load alone."},{"t":"Wait for someone else to start.","f":"You can be the one who starts!"}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"figtree","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 3 of With Christ in the School of Prayer in real life."},{"sc":"figtree","n":"🌳 Have faith in God. Look at Him, not the problem."},{"sc":"college","n":"⛰️ Pray God's promises with confidence."},{"sc":"prayercloset","n":"🤲 Forgive when you pray."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"🤝 Pray together with friends."}],"stops":{"mu3s1":{"story":[{"sc":"figtree","n":"One morning, on the way into Jerusalem, Jesus was hungry. He saw a {fig tree} covered in leaves, but when He looked, there was no fruit on it at all."},{"sc":"figtree","w":"amjesus","e":"stern","t":"No man eat fruit of thee hereafter for ever."},{"sc":"figtree","n":"The next morning, as they walked past again, the disciples stared. The fig tree had dried up from the roots."},{"sc":"figtree","w":"ampeter","e":"shock","t":"Master, behold, the fig tree which thou cursedst is withered away."},{"sc":"figtree","w":"amjesus","e":"smile","t":"Have faith in God."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Notice what Jesus didn't say. He didn't say 'have faith in your faith' or 'have faith in your feelings'. He said: have faith in God."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"big","t":"Faith isn't trying hard to feel sure. It's looking away from the problem, and looking at God: how great He is, how good He is, and how faithful He's always been."},{"sc":"home","w":"amemeka","e":"smile","t":"So when I'm worried, instead of staring at the worry, I look at who God is."}],"quote":{"text":"And Jesus answering saith unto them, Have faith in God.","who":"Mark 11:22","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Look at God, not the problem","text":"After the fig tree withered, Jesus said: 'Have faith in God.' Murray says faith isn't forcing a feeling. It's looking away from the problem and looking at God: how great, good and faithful He is."},"think":"What worry are you staring at right now? What do you know about God that's bigger than it?","quiz":[{"q":"What was missing from the fig tree?","o":["Fruit","Leaves","Roots","Branches"],"why":"It was covered in leaves but had no fruit."},{"q":"What had happened to the fig tree the next morning?","o":["It had dried up from the roots","It was full of fruit","It had moved","Nothing"],"why":"The disciples were amazed."},{"q":"Who pointed out the withered tree?","o":["Peter","John","Judas","Thomas"],"why":"\"Master, behold...\""},{"q":"What did Jesus say in reply?","o":["\"Have faith in God\"","\"Be afraid\"","\"Plant another tree\"","\"Never mind\""],"why":"Mark 11:22."},{"q":"What did Murray say faith is?","o":["Looking away from the problem and looking at God","Feeling very sure","Having faith in your feelings","Ignoring problems"],"why":"Faith looks at who God is."}]},"mu3s2":{"story":[{"sc":"figtree","w":"amjesus","e":"big","t":"Whosoever shall say unto this mountain, Be thou removed, and be thou cast into the sea; and shall not doubt in his heart, but shall believe... he shall have whatsoever he saith."},{"sc":"figtree","w":"amjesus","e":"smile","t":"Therefore I say unto you, What things soever ye desire, when ye pray, believe that ye receive them, and ye shall have them."},{"sc":"home","w":"amemeka","e":"smirk","t":"So if I pray for a new phone and really, really believe, I'll get one?"},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Ha! Careful, Emeka. Faith isn't a magic trick for getting whatever we want. The Bible also says: if we ask anything according to His will, He hears us."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Faith grows from God's word. When you find a promise in the Bible, like 'If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God', you can pray for it with full confidence."},{"sc":"college","n":"Emeka had to speak in front of the whole school at assembly. He was terrified. He found the promise in James about wisdom, and prayed for wisdom and courage, believing God would give them."},{"sc":"college","n":"His knees still shook a little. But the words came clearly, and he finished strong."},{"sc":"college","w":"amemeka","e":"big","t":"I asked for something God promised. And He gave it!"}],"quote":{"text":"And this is the confidence that we have in him, that, if we ask any thing according to his will, he heareth us.","who":"1 John 5:14","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Faith stands on God's promises","text":"Jesus said: believe that you receive, and you shall have. Murray explains that faith isn't a magic trick. It grows from God's word and His will. Find His promises and pray them with confidence."},"think":"Find one promise of God in the Bible. Write it down and pray it this week.","quiz":[{"q":"What did Jesus say faith could move?","o":["A mountain","A chair","A house","A boat"],"why":"Into the sea!"},{"q":"What did Emeka first want to pray for?","o":["A new phone","Wisdom","His friends","Rain"],"why":"Murray said: careful!"},{"q":"According to 1 John 5:14, God hears us when we ask...","o":["According to His will","Very loudly","Many times","With big words"],"why":"That's our confidence."},{"q":"What did Emeka pray for before assembly?","o":["Wisdom and courage","A day off","That assembly would be cancelled","A new phone"],"why":"From the promise in James."},{"q":"Where does faith grow from, according to Murray?","o":["God's word and promises","Feelings","Luck","Money"],"why":"Pray His promises."}]},"mu3s3":{"story":[{"sc":"college","n":"Joy had told the whole class that Ladi had copied her homework. It wasn't true, and everyone believed it."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"amladi","e":"frown","t":"I tried to pray tonight, but all I could think about was Joy. I'm so angry with her. My prayers feel like they're hitting the ceiling."},{"sc":"figtree","w":"amjesus","e":"smile","t":"And when ye stand praying, forgive, if ye have ought against any: that your Father also which is in heaven may forgive you your trespasses."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Right after teaching about faith, Jesus spoke about forgiveness. I noticed this: prayer and love go together. A heart full of bitterness finds it hard to pray."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"amladi","e":"worried","t":"But what she did was wrong! Do I have to pretend it didn't happen?"},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"No. Forgiving doesn't mean it didn't matter, or that you must trust her straight away. It means you hand it over to God, let go of revenge, and choose to wish her good. And God helps you do it."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"amladi","e":"worried","t":"Lord, I forgive Joy. It's hard. Please help me mean it. And please help her too."},{"sc":"college","n":"A week later, Joy came to Ladi in tears and admitted she'd made it up because she was jealous. Ladi was able to say, 'I've already forgiven you.' Joy couldn't believe it."}],"quote":{"text":"And when ye stand praying, forgive, if ye have ought against any.","who":"Mark 11:25","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Prayer and love go together","text":"Ladi couldn't pray because of her anger at Joy. Jesus said: when you pray, forgive. Forgiving doesn't mean the wrong didn't matter. It means handing it to God, letting go of revenge, and choosing to wish them good, with God's help."},"think":"Is there someone you need to forgive before you pray? Ask God to help you, even if it's hard.","quiz":[{"q":"What had Joy falsely said about Ladi?","o":["That she copied her homework","That she stole a pen","That she was late","That she cheated at football"],"why":"And everyone believed it."},{"q":"Why did Ladi's prayers feel stuck?","o":["She was full of anger","She was tired","She forgot the words","It was too noisy"],"why":"Bitterness makes prayer hard."},{"q":"What did Jesus say to do when you stand praying?","o":["Forgive","Shout","Kneel only","Close the door"],"why":"Mark 11:25."},{"q":"Does forgiving mean the wrong didn't matter?","o":["No, it means handing it to God and letting go of revenge","Yes","It means pretending","It means forgetting instantly"],"why":"And choosing to wish them good."},{"q":"What happened when Joy apologised?","o":["Ladi said she had already forgiven her","Ladi refused","Ladi told the teacher","Nothing"],"why":"Joy couldn't believe it!"}]},"mu3s4":{"story":[{"sc":"prison","n":"King Herod had arrested Peter and thrown him into prison, chained between two soldiers. The plan was to kill him after the festival."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"But the church gathered at Mary's house, and they prayed without ceasing for Peter, late into the night."},{"sc":"prison","n":"That very night, an angel appeared in the cell. Peter's chains fell off. The iron gate of the city opened all by itself!"},{"sc":"knockdoor","w":"ampeter","e":"big","t":"(Knock, knock!) Open up! It's me, Peter!"},{"sc":"knockdoor","n":"A servant girl called Rhoda ran to the door. When she heard Peter's voice, she was so excited that she forgot to open it, and ran back inside!"},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"amrhoda","e":"big","t":"It's Peter! Peter is at the door!"},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"'You're mad!' they said. But Peter kept knocking. When they finally opened the door, they were astonished. God had answered their prayer while they were still praying."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Jesus promised: if two of you agree on earth about anything you ask, it shall be done for them by my Father. There's special power when God's people pray together."},{"sc":"home","w":"amemeka","e":"big","t":"Ladi, let's start a prayer group at school. Even if it's just two or three of us!"}],"quote":{"text":"For where two or three are gathered together in my name, there am I in the midst of them.","who":"Matthew 18:20","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Pray together","text":"The church prayed together for Peter, and God opened the prison, so fast that Rhoda forgot to open the door! Jesus promised special power when two or three agree in prayer. Find a friend and pray together."},"think":"Who could you pray with regularly? What could you agree together to pray about?","proverb":{"text":"Àjèjé ọwọ́ kan kò gbé ẹrù dórí.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"One hand alone cannot lift a load onto the head. We do much more together than alone."},"quiz":[{"q":"Who put Peter in prison?","o":["King Herod","Pharaoh","Nebuchadnezzar","Caesar"],"why":"Chained between two soldiers."},{"q":"What was the church doing while Peter was in prison?","o":["Praying together without ceasing","Sleeping","Hiding","Arguing"],"why":"At Mary's house."},{"q":"What did Rhoda forget to do?","o":["Open the door","Say hello","Put the kettle on","Close the window"],"why":"She was so excited!"},{"q":"What did Jesus promise if two agree in prayer?","o":["It shall be done by my Father","Nothing happens","Only one gets an answer","They'll argue"],"why":"Matthew 18:19."},{"q":"What does the Yoruba proverb say one hand can't do?","o":["Lift a load onto the head","Wave","Write","Clap softly"],"why":"Together is stronger."}]}}},"mu4":{"challenge":[{"q":"Jesus said the harvest is plenteous but the labourers are...?","o":["few","many","lazy","tired"],"why":"Matthew 9:37."},{"q":"What did Jesus tell us to pray for in Matthew 9:38?","o":["Labourers for the harvest","Rain","Money","A bigger barn"],"why":"Pray the Lord of the harvest."},{"q":"What word did Murray love most?","o":["Abide","Hurry","Win","Rest"],"why":"Stay close to Jesus."},{"q":"Without abiding in the vine, a branch can't...?","o":["Bear fruit","Grow leaves","Fall","Sway"],"why":"John 15:4."},{"q":"What did Emeka do when the school bell rang?","o":["Whispered 'Jesus, I'm still with You'","Ran home","Fell asleep","Ignored it"],"why":"Abiding all day."},{"q":"What did the principal give Emeka?","o":["A signed note","A sports kit","A detention","A prize"],"why":"His name opened the door."},{"q":"Praying in Jesus' name means coming on whose account?","o":["Jesus'","Our own","Our parents'","Our teachers'"],"why":"His name, not ours."},{"q":"John 16:24: ask, that your ___ may be full.","o":["joy","bag","house","stomach"],"why":"Ask and receive."},{"q":"In what year did Andrew Murray die?","o":["1917","1828","1860","2000"],"why":"Aged 88."},{"q":"\"Pray without...\"","o":["ceasing","thinking","friends","words"],"why":"1 Thessalonians 5:17."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What does 'supplication' mean?","o":["Asking God humbly and earnestly","Singing loudly","Sleeping","Eating"],"why":"Ephesians 6:18."},"choices":[{"title":"A friend far from God","q":"Your best friend says she doesn't believe in God.","o":[{"t":"Keep being a good friend, and pray for her every day by name.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Pray the Lord of the harvest."},{"t":"Stop being friends.","f":"Love her and pray for her."},{"t":"Argue until she agrees.","f":"Prayer and kindness open hearts more than arguments."}]},{"title":"Busy day","q":"You're so busy with school and chores that you forget about God until bedtime.","o":[{"t":"Use a small reminder to talk to Jesus through the day.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Abide in Him all day."},{"t":"Only think about God on Sundays.","f":"Abiding is for every day."},{"t":"Give up trying.","f":"Even a whisper keeps you close."}]},{"title":"Selfish prayer","q":"You want to pray, 'In Jesus' name, make my rival fail his exam.'","o":[{"t":"Ask: would Jesus sign His name to this? Pray for yourself to do well instead.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Ask what glorifies the Father."},{"t":"Pray it anyway.","f":"You can't forge Jesus' signature!"},{"t":"Pray for something worse.","f":"That's not His name's character."}]},{"title":"School's out","q":"You've finished this book. You think, \"I've learned prayer now. Done!\"","o":[{"t":"Keep learning: in Jesus' school of prayer, we never graduate.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Pray always, and never stop."},{"t":"Stop praying now.","f":"Prayer runs through all of life."},{"t":"Only pray when you need something.","f":"Pray without ceasing, and give thanks."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"wheatfield","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use With Christ in the School of Prayer in real life."},{"sc":"wheatfield","n":"🌾 Pray for workers in the harvest, and be ready to go."},{"sc":"vineyard","n":"🍇 Abide in Jesus all day long."},{"sc":"college","n":"✉️ Pray in Jesus' name: ask what He'd sign His name to."},{"sc":"prayercloset","n":"🔄 Pray always, and never stop learning."}],"stops":{"mu4s1":{"story":[{"sc":"multitude","n":"Jesus travelled through towns and villages, teaching and healing. Everywhere He went, crowds followed Him."},{"sc":"multitude","n":"When He saw the crowds, He was moved with compassion for them. They were tired and scattered, like sheep without a shepherd."},{"sc":"wheatfield","w":"amjesus","e":"smile","t":"The harvest truly is plenteous, but the {labourers} are few; Pray ye therefore the Lord of the harvest, that he will send forth labourers into his harvest."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Did you notice? Jesus didn't first say 'Go!' He said 'Pray!' Before anyone is sent, someone must pray."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"big","t":"I saw it happen. After the revival in 1860, many young men offered themselves to become pastors and missionaries. People had been praying for workers for years."},{"sc":"home","w":"amladi","e":"smile","t":"So I can be part of the harvest just by praying? Even before I go anywhere?"},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Yes! Pray for missionaries by name. Pray for your friends who don't know Jesus yet. And be ready: sometimes God answers the prayer by sending you!"},{"sc":"home","n":"Ladi and Emeka found the names of two missionaries their church supports, one in northern Nigeria and one in Niger, and wrote them on their prayer list."}],"quote":{"text":"But when he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion on them, because they fainted, and were scattered abroad, as sheep having no shepherd.","who":"Matthew 9:36","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Pray before you go","text":"Jesus saw the crowds, felt compassion, and said: pray for workers! Murray saw God answer that prayer in South Africa. You can be part of the harvest by praying, for missionaries, for friends, and by being ready if God sends you."},"think":"Who is one friend who doesn't know Jesus yet? Add them to your prayer list today.","quiz":[{"q":"How did Jesus feel when He saw the crowds?","o":["Moved with compassion","Annoyed","Tired","Bored"],"why":"Like sheep without a shepherd."},{"q":"What did Jesus say about the harvest?","o":["It is plenteous, but labourers are few","It is small","It is finished","It is not ready"],"why":"Matthew 9:37."},{"q":"What did Jesus tell us to do first?","o":["Pray the Lord of the harvest","Go immediately","Wait","Build barns"],"why":"Before going, pray."},{"q":"What happened after the 1860 revival?","o":["Many young men offered to become pastors and missionaries","Nothing","Everyone moved away","The church closed"],"why":"God answered prayers for workers."},{"q":"How did Murray say God sometimes answers prayers for workers?","o":["By sending you!","Never","With money only","By sending angels only"],"why":"Be ready."}]},"mu4s2":{"story":[{"sc":"vineyard","w":"amjesus","e":"smile","t":"If ye abide in me, and my words abide in you, ye shall ask what ye will, and it shall be done unto you."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"This was one of my favourite words in all the Bible: {abide}. Stay. Remain. Live close. I even wrote a whole book about it."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Here's the secret. When we abide in Jesus, and His words fill our minds, we start to want what He wants. Our prayers begin to match His heart. And those are the prayers He loves to answer."},{"sc":"prayercloset","n":"For a time, Murray lost his voice and couldn't preach at all. It was a hard season. But he said it taught him to rest in Jesus, and not to depend on his own strength or gifts."},{"sc":"home","w":"amemeka","e":"worried","t":"But how do I abide in Jesus when I'm at school, doing maths, playing football?"},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Abiding isn't only for quiet times. It's remembering He's with you all day: talking to Him in your head, trusting Him in small things, obeying Him when it's hard. Like a branch that never lets go of the vine."},{"sc":"college","n":"Emeka started a small habit: every time the school bell rang, he whispered, 'Jesus, I'm still with You.' By the end of the term, he felt closer to God than ever."}],"quote":{"text":"Abide in me, and I in you. As the branch cannot bear fruit of itself, except it abide in the vine; no more can ye, except ye abide in me.","who":"John 15:4","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Stay close, pray His heart","text":"Jesus promised: if you abide in Me and My words abide in you, ask what you will. Staying close to Jesus changes what we want, so our prayers match His heart. Abiding is for all day, not just quiet times."},"think":"What small reminder, like Emeka's school bell, could help you remember Jesus throughout your day?","quiz":[{"q":"What does 'abide' mean?","o":["Stay, remain and live close","Run away","Forget","Sleep"],"why":"Murray's favourite word."},{"q":"What happens to our prayers when we abide in Jesus?","o":["They begin to match His heart","They stop","They get longer","Nothing"],"why":"We want what He wants."},{"q":"What happened to Murray for a time?","o":["He lost his voice and couldn't preach","He became king","He moved to Nigeria","He stopped praying"],"why":"It taught him to rest in Jesus."},{"q":"What did Emeka whisper when the school bell rang?","o":["\"Jesus, I'm still with You\"","\"Hooray, lunch!\"","\"Oh no\"","Nothing"],"why":"Abiding all day long."},{"q":"Complete John 15:7: \"If ye abide in me, and my words abide in you...\"","o":["ye shall ask what ye will, and it shall be done","ye shall be rich","ye shall never be sad","ye shall sleep well"],"why":"Abide, then ask."}]},"mu4s3":{"story":[{"sc":"upperroom","n":"On the night before He died, Jesus sat with His disciples and gave them an amazing promise."},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"amjesus","e":"smile","t":"And whatsoever ye shall ask in my name, that will I do, that the Father may be glorified in the Son. If ye shall ask any thing in my name, I will do it."},{"sc":"college","n":"That week, Emeka needed to get a sports kit from the staff room. Students weren't allowed in. The teachers shook their heads."},{"sc":"college","w":"amprincipal","e":"smile","t":"Here, Emeka. Take this note. I've signed it."},{"sc":"college","n":"Emeka showed the note at the staff room door. The teacher read the principal's signature and immediately let him in."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"That's what praying 'in Jesus' name' means. It isn't a magic phrase we tack on at the end. It means we come to the Father on Jesus' account, not our own. His name opens the door."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"big","t":"But it also means asking for the things Jesus would sign His name to: things that bring glory to the Father. You wouldn't forge the principal's name for something he'd never allow!"},{"sc":"home","w":"amladi","e":"smile","t":"So before I say 'in Jesus' name', I can ask: would Jesus sign His name to this prayer?"}],"quote":{"text":"Hitherto have ye asked nothing in my name: ask, and ye shall receive, that your joy may be full.","who":"John 16:24","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"On Jesus' account","text":"Emeka got into the staff room because of the principal's signed note. Praying in Jesus' name means coming to the Father on His account, not ours. It also means asking for what Jesus would sign His name to: things that glorify the Father."},"think":"Next time you end a prayer 'in Jesus' name', stop and ask: would Jesus sign His name to this?","quiz":[{"q":"When did Jesus give the promise about His name?","o":["The night before He died","At His birth","At a wedding","On a boat"],"why":"In the upper room."},{"q":"How did Emeka get into the staff room?","o":["With a note signed by the principal","By climbing in","By shouting","He didn't"],"why":"The signature opened the door."},{"q":"Is 'in Jesus' name' a magic phrase?","o":["No, it means coming on Jesus' account","Yes","It's just a habit","It doesn't mean anything"],"why":"His name opens the door."},{"q":"What should we ask for in Jesus' name?","o":["Things He would sign His name to","Anything selfish","Only money","Nothing"],"why":"That the Father may be glorified."},{"q":"According to John 16:24, why should we ask?","o":["That our joy may be full","To be famous","To be rich","To impress people"],"why":"Ask, and ye shall receive."}]},"mu4s4":{"story":[{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"smile","t":"Our last lesson. Paul wrote: praying always, with all prayer and {supplication}, for all the saints. Prayer isn't one subject in the school of life. It runs through every subject."},{"sc":"karoo","n":"Andrew Murray lived this way for a very long life. He pastored churches across South Africa, led his church in many big decisions, and helped start a school where girls could get a good education."},{"sc":"karoo","n":"He wrote more than two hundred books. He called Christians everywhere to pray for missions, and he prayed for them himself, day after day."},{"sc":"karoo","n":"In 1917, at the age of 88, Andrew Murray went home to be with the Lord in the town of Wellington, South Africa. His books on prayer are still read all over the world."},{"sc":"prayercloset","w":"murray","e":"big","t":"But don't remember me. Remember the Teacher! Ask, seek, knock. Trust your Father. Forgive. Pray with friends. Abide in Jesus. Ask in His name. And never, ever stop."},{"sc":"home","w":"amemeka","e":"big","t":"Lord, teach us to pray. We want to stay in Your school forever!"},{"sc":"home","w":"amladi","e":"smile","t":"Same time tomorrow, on the back step?"},{"sc":"home","w":"amemeka","e":"big","t":"Same time tomorrow!"}],"quote":{"text":"Pray without ceasing. In every thing give thanks: for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus concerning you.","who":"1 Thessalonians 5:17-18","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Never stop learning","text":"Prayer runs through all of life, not just one part. Murray prayed and called others to pray for over sixty years. His last word to you: remember the Teacher, and never stop praying."},"think":"Look back at all you've learned in this book. Which lesson do you most want to practise this month?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Murray compare prayer to in the school of life?","o":["Something that runs through every subject","One subject only","A holiday","A test"],"why":"Pray always."},{"q":"What kind of school did Murray help start?","o":["A school where girls could get a good education","A cricket school","A cooking school","A dance school"],"why":"In Wellington."},{"q":"How old was Murray when he died?","o":["88","40","54","100"],"why":"In 1917."},{"q":"Who did Murray want us to remember most?","o":["The Teacher, Jesus","Murray himself","His father","Nobody"],"why":"Lord, teach us to pray."},{"q":"What does Ephesians 6:18 tell us to do?","o":["Pray always","Pray once a year","Pray only when sad","Never pray"],"why":"With all perseverance."}]}}}});
